    <section class="faq wrap">
        <p class="eyebrow">A FEW USEFUL ANSWERS</p>
        <h2>Before you start.</h2>
        <details>
            <summary>Is AKML free?</summary>
            <p>AKML is MIT-licensed and free to use. Your chosen AI provider may charge separately for its service.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
            <summary>Can I use PostgreSQL inside SSMS?</summary>
            <p>AKML's PostgreSQL workflow is in the browser edition with a compatible connected engine. The SSMS 22 extension is for SQL Server.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
            <summary>Does the browser edition need an engine?</summary>
            <p>Database connections and query execution require the engine. PostgreSQL language services also require it. SQL Server formatting and analysis can run locally in the browser.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
            <summary>Do I need to use AI?</summary>
            <p>No. Completion, formatting, analysis and SQL history provide useful workflows without configuring an AI provider.</p>
        </details>
    </section>
